Releases the tiles of a layer, or a source, that stops rendering. When the
camera leaves a layer's zoom range, the renderer stops preparing and updating
the layer, but the layer kept the tiles it last rendered, and so did its
drawables. Those tiles hold their whole layout results, with the CPU and GPU
buffers of every bucket, so zooming out of a city kept its buildings, roads,
and labels after the source dropped their tiles, even with the tile cache
disabled. A source whose layers were all out of range kept its last tiles the
same way, since only enabled sources are prepared.

RenderLayer::markLayerRenderable() now removes the drawables and drops the
tiles and placement data of a layer that stops rendering. The layer's next
prepare() and update() rebuild them, as they do after a tile changes. A
disabled RenderTileSource drops its tiles through the new
RenderSource::releaseRenderData().
Upstream: not proposed

